        "content": "\n          <p>Safety is paramount whenever traveling outside your university town. Never compromise on personal security to save a few coins:</p>\n          <p><strong>1. Share Your Live Itinerary with a Trusted Friend:</strong> Always inform your roommate or lodge executive of your exact destination, accommodation contact, and expected return time. Share live WhatsApp location tracking during transit.</p>\n          <p><strong>2. Travel During Broad Daylight:</strong> Avoid late-night inter-city transit. Depart early on Saturday morning so you arrive at your destination before midday, allowing ample daylight to inspect accommodation.</p>\n          <p><strong>3. Verify Lodging Cleanliness and Security:</strong> If staying overnight, verify reviews online or call ahead. Choose well-lit, gated guest houses with verified security personnel rather than isolated, obscure rentals.</p>\n        \n      <p>Thorough preparation is the secret to stress-free budget travel. Assemble a compact student travel kit containing power banks, reusable water flasks, basic first-aid supplies, and offline digital maps. Being self-sufficient eliminates unexpected on-the-road expenses and ensures smooth navigation.</p>\n    "
